        answer: "Only if the AHJ allows it, and most do not want phased correction responses — they want one complete resubmittal that answers every comment, because partial responses create version-control chaos on their side. A few jurisdictions accept phased resubmittals on large projects by prior agreement, but I never assume it. The faster play is a complete, well-organized resubmittal: every comment answered in a response letter keyed to clouded revisions on the re-sealed sheets. Reviewers reward clarity — a resubmittal they can verify in one pass goes back out faster than one they have to decode.",
